              "@id": "urn:uuid:f031c3b0-ad1f-5663-8472-34d7864c91d3",
              "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedString",
              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nCAT B,CLOSED\n\nU.S. District Court\nDistrict of Columbia (Washington, DC)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 1:22-cr-00150-JEB All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. PATHMANATHAN Date Filed: 05/02/2022\n\nAssigned to: Chief Judge James E. Boasberg\n\nDefendant (1)\nRAMANAN PATHMANATHAN represented by Diane Aimee Shrewsbury\nOFFICE OF THE FEDERAL PUBLIC DEFENDER FOR THE DISTRICT OF CO\n625 Indiana Avenue NW\nSuite 550\nWashington, DC 20004\n(202) 208-7500\nFax: (202) 208-7515\nEmail: diane_shrewsbury@fd.org\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender Appointment\n\nAlexis Morgan Gardner\nFEDERAL PUBLIC DEFENDER FOR THE DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA\n625 Indiana Ave,NW\nSuite 500\nWashington, DC 20004\n(202) 208-7500\nEmail: alexis_gardner@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 01/14/2026\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender Appointment\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:2251(a),(e) and 18:3238; SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN; Sexual Exploitation Defendant sentenced to three hundred sixty (360) months incarceration to run concurrent to\nof a Child Count 11 and consecutive to any other sentence imposed, followed by a ten (10) year term of\n(5) Supervised Release to run concurrent to Count 11, and a $100 Special Assessment.\n18:2422(b) and 18:3238; COERCION OR ENTICEMENT OF FEMALE; Coercion and Defendant sentenced to three hundred ninety-six (396) months incarceration to run concurrent to\nEnticement of a Minor Count 5 and consecutive to any other sentence imposed, followed by a ten (10) year term of\n(11) Supervised Release to run concurrent to Count 5, and a $100 Special Assessment.\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\n18:2251(a),(e) and 18:3238; SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN; Sexual Exploitation\nof a Child DISMISSED ON ORAL MOTION BY THE GOVERNMENT.\n(1-4)\n18:2251(a),(e) and 18:3238; SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN; Sexual Exploitation\nof a Child DISMISSED ON ORAL MOTION BY THE GOVERNMENT.\n(6-10)\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nFelony\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Amy Elizabeth Larson\nUNITED STATES ATTORNEY'S OFFICE\n555 4th Street, NW\nWashington, DC 20530\n(202) 252-7863\nEmail: amy.larson2@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant U.S. Attorney\n\nKaren Shinskie\nU.S. ATTORNEY'S OFFICE\n601 D Street NW\nWashington, DC 20530\n202-252-7688\nEmail: karen.shinskie@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant U.S. Attorney\n\nKaylynn Foulon\nDOJ-CRM\n1301 New York Avenue NW\nSte 11th Floor\nWashington, DC 20005\n301-992-7384\nEmail: kaylynn.foulon@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Assistant U.S. Attorney\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n05/02/2022 1 SEALED INDICTMENT as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1) count(s) 1-10, 11. (FORFEITURE ALLEAGATIONS). (zstd) (Main Document 1 replaced on 12/3/2025) (znmw). (Entered: 05/02/2022)\n05/02/2022 3 MOTION to Seal Case by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (Attachments: # 1 Text of Proposed Order)(zstd) (Main Document 3 replaced on 12/3/2025) (znmw). (Attachment 1 replaced on 12/3/2025) (znmw).\n(Entered: 05/02/2022)\n05/02/2022 4 ORDER granting 3 Motion to Seal Case as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1). Signed by Magistrate Judge Robin M. Meriweather on 5/4/2022. (zstd) (Main Document 4 replaced on 12/3/2025) (znmw). (Entered:\n05/02/2022)\n01/11/2023 5 Case as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN directly reassigned to the Calendar Committee as defendant is a fugitive. Judge James E. Boasberg is no longer assigned to the case. (ztnr) (Main Document 5 replaced on\n12/3/2025) (znmw). (Entered: 01/12/2023)\n12/03/2025 Arrest of RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (znjb) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 6 Arrest Warrant Returned Executed on 12/3/2025 as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (znjb) (Main Document 6 replaced on 12/3/2025) (znmw). (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 7 Case as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN directly reassigned to Chief Judge James E. Boasberg as the defendant is no longer a fugitive. Calendar Committee is no longer assigned to the case. (rj) (Main Document 7\nreplaced on 12/3/2025) (znmw). (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 Case unsealed as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (znmw) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 ORAL MOTION to Appoint Counsel by RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (znjb) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 ORAL MOTION for Temporary Detention by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (znjb) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 ORAL MOTION for Speedy Trial by USA, RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (znjb) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Magistrate Judge Moxila A. Upadhyaya: Return on Arrest Warrant/Initial Appearance/Arraignment as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN held on 12/3/2025. Not Guilty Plea\nentered as to Counts 1-10,11. The Court advised the Government of its Due Process Obligations under Rule 5(f). Notice of Right to Consular Notification given to defendant; defendant request notification. Oral Motion to\nAppoint Counsel as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN; heard and granted. Oral Motion by the Government for Temporary Detention (3 day hold) as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN; heard and granted. Defendant\nConceded to detention. Waives written findings of fact, and reserves the right to address any future requests for release before the assigned District Judge. Joint Oral Motion for Speedy Trial as to RAMANAN\nPATHMANATHAN; heard and granted. Speedy Trial Excluded between 12/3/2025 to 12/10/2025 in the Interest of Justice (XT). Status Conference set for 12/10/2025 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 22A- In Person before\nChief Judge James E. Boasberg. Bond Status of Defendant: Defendant Committed/Commitment Issued; Court Reporter: FTR- GOLD; FTR Time Frame: CRTM 5: [2:03:53-2:12:30]; Defense Attorney: Alexis Gardner; US\nAttorney: Karen Shinskie; Pretrial Officer: Britney Dahlkoetter. (znjb) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN: As required by Rule 5(f), the United States is ordered to produce all exculpatory evidence to the defendant pursuant to Brady v. Maryland and its progeny. Not\ndoing so in a timely manner may result in sanctions, including exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges and contempt proceedings. Signed by Magistrate Judge Moxila A. Upadhyaya on\n12/3/2025. (znjb) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 10 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Karen Shinskie appearing for USA. (Shinskie, Karen) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 11 Consent MOTION for Protective Order by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (Shinskie, Karen) (Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/03/2025 12 Consent MOTION for Order Disclose Information Protected by Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 6(e) by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (Shinskie, Karen) Modified event type on 12/4/2025 (zstd).\n(Entered: 12/03/2025)\n12/04/2025 13 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Kaylynn Foulon appearing for USA. (Foulon, Kaylynn) (Entered: 12/04/2025)\n12/04/2025 14 ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1), GRANTING 11 Motion for Protective Order. Signed by Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on December 4, 2025. (znbn) (Entered: 12/04/2025)\n12/04/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1), GRANTING 12 Consent Motion for Order to Disclose Information Protected by Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 6(e). So ORDERED by Chief Judge\nJames E. Boasberg on December 4, 2025. (znbn) (Entered: 12/04/2025)\n12/04/2025 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1): Pursuant to the Due Process Protections Act, the Court ORDERS that all government counsel shall review their disclosure obligations under Brady v.\nMaryland, 373 U.S. 83 (1963), and its progeny, as set forth in Local Criminal Rule 5.1, and comply with those provisions. The failure to comply could result in dismissal of the indictment or information, dismissal of\nindividual charges, exclusion of government evidence or witnesses, continuances, Bar discipline, or any other remedy that is just under the circumstances. So ORDERED by Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on December 4,\n2025. (znbn) (Entered: 12/04/2025)\n12/10/2025 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Chief Judge James E. Boasberg: Status Conference as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1) held on December 10, 2025. Plea Agreement Hearing set for January 28, 2026, at\n11:00 AM in Courtroom 22A- In Person before Chief Judge James E. Boasberg. The Court will toll the Speedy Trial Clock between December 10, 2025, and January 28, 2026 (XT). Bond Status of Defendant:\nCOMMITTED/COMMITMENT ISSUED; Court Reporter: Tammy Nestor; Defense Attorney: Alexis Gardner; US Attorney: Kaylynn Foulon and Karen Shinskie. (znbn) (Entered: 12/10/2025)\n12/10/2025 15 NOTICE of Discovery Production by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (Attachments: # 1 Supplement)(Shinskie, Karen) (Entered: 12/10/2025)\n01/14/2026 16 NOTICE OF SUBSTITUTION OF COUNSEL Attorney Shrewsbury, Diane Aimee added. (Shrewsbury, Diane) (Entered: 01/14/2026)\n01/16/2026 17 Consent MOTION to Continue Plea Hearing by RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (Shrewsbury, Diane) (Entered: 01/16/2026)\n01/20/2026 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1), GRANTING 17 Motion to Continue: The Court ORDERS that the Plea Agreement Hearing set for January 28, 2026, is VACATED and RESET to January 30,\n2026, at 11:00 AM in Courtroom 22A- In Person before Chief Judge James E. Boasberg. The Court will toll the Speedy Trial Clock between January 20, 2026, and January 30, 2026. So ORDERED by Chief Judge James E.\nBoasberg on January 20, 2026. (znbn) (Entered: 01/20/2026)\n01/30/2026 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Chief Judge James E. Boasberg: Plea Agreement Hearing as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1) held on January 30, 2026. Defendant sworn and entered a plea of GUILTY as\nto counts five (5) and eleven (11) of the Indictment filed on May 2, 2022. The Court accepts the plea and the defendant is adjudged GUILTY. REFERRAL TO PROBATION OFFICE for Presentence Investigation as to\nRAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1). Sentencing set for May 27, 2026 at 11:00 AM in Courtroom 22A- In Person before Chief Judge James E. Boasberg. Bond Status of Defendant: COMMITTED/COMMITMENT\nISSUED; Court Reporter: Tammy Nestor; Defense Attorney: Diane Shrewsbury; US Attorney: Karen Shinskie. (znbn) (Entered: 01/30/2026)\n01/30/2026 18 WAIVER of Trial by Jury as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1). Approved by Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on January 30, 2026. (znbn) (Entered: 01/30/2026)\n01/30/2026 19 PLEA AGREEMENT as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1). (znbn) (Entered: 01/30/2026)\n01/30/2026 20 STATEMENT OF OFFENSE by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1). (znbn) (Entered: 01/30/2026)\n05/13/2026 26 Unopposed MOTION for Leave to Appear by Telephone or Video for Victims at Sentencing by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (Shinskie, Karen) (Entered: 05/13/2026)\n05/13/2026 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1), granting 26 Motion for Leave to Appear by Telephone or Video for Victims at Sentencing. So ORDERED by Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on May 13,\n2026. (znbn) (Entered: 05/13/2026)\n05/20/2026 27 SENTENCING MEMORANDUM by USA as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (Shinskie, Karen) (Entered: 05/20/2026)\n05/21/2026 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1), granting 29 Sealed Motion for Leave to File Document Under Seal (This document is SEALED and only available to authorized persons.). So ORDERED by\nChief Judge James E. Boasberg on May 21, 2026. (znbn) (Entered: 05/21/2026)\n05/26/2026 32 Unopposed MOTION for Family to Attend Sentencing via Zoom by RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (Shrewsbury, Diane) (Entered: 05/26/2026)\n05/26/2026 33 MOTION to Remove all Restraints at Court Proceedings by RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. (Shrewsbury, Diane) (Entered: 05/26/2026)\n05/26/2026 34 SENTENCING MEMORANDUM by RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit B, # 2 Exhibit C)(Shrewsbury, Diane) (Entered: 05/26/2026)\n05/26/2026 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1), granting 32 Unopposed Motion for Family to Attend Sentencing via Zoom. So ORDERED by Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on May 26, 2026. (znbn)\n(Entered: 05/26/2026)\n05/26/2026 MINUTE ORDER as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1), granting 33 Motion to Remove all Restraints at Court Proceedings. So ORDERED by Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on May 26, 2026. (znbn) (Entered:\n05/26/2026)\n05/27/2026 Minute Entry for proceedings held before Chief Judge James E. Boasberg: Sentencing as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN (1) held on May 27, 2026. As set forth on the record, the Court will accept the 11(c)1(C) plea. It\nis the judgment of the Court, as to Counts 5 and 11, that the defendant is hereby committed to the custody of the Bureau of Prisons for a term of three hundred ninety-six (396) months. Defendant sentenced to three hundred\nsixty (360) months incarceration as to Count 5, three hundred ninety-six (396) months incarceration on Count 11 to run concurrent to each other and consecutive to any other sentence imposed. Defendant is further\nsentenced to a ten (10) year term of Supervised Release as to Counts 5 and 11 to run concurrently, followed by Special Assessments totaling $200. For the reasons stated on the record, the Court will delay the imposition of\nrestitution. The Court ORDERS that the parties file a Consent Order on Restitution by August 27, 2026. No fine imposed. Oral motion by the Government to \"dismiss the remaining counts\" GRANTED. The Court\nORDERS that Counts 1-4 and 6-10 are DISMISSED. Appeal rights given. Bond Status of Defendant: COMMITTED/COMMITMENT ISSUED; Court Reporter: Tammy Nestor; Defense Attorney: Diane Shrewsbury; US\nAttorney: Karen Shinskie; Prob Officer: Sarah Asbury-Baca; Government Witnesses: seven (7) victims. (znbn) Modified to add dismissed counts on 5/28/2026 (znbn). (Entered: 05/27/2026)\n05/27/2026 37 JUDGMENT as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN. Statement of Reasons Not Included. Signed by Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on 5/27/2026. (zstd) (Entered: 05/28/2026)\n05/27/2026 38 STATEMENT OF REASONS as to RAMANAN PATHMANATHAN re 37 Judgment Access to the PDF Document is restricted per Judicial Conference Policy. Access is limited to Counsel of Record and the Court. Signed\nby Chief Judge James E. Boasberg on 5/27/2026. (zstd) (Entered: 05/28/2026)\n\nPACER Service Center\nTransaction Receipt\n06/20/2026 01:41:59\nPACER\nmrinaal_ramachandran Client Code:\nLogin:\nSearch 1:22-cr-00150-\nDescription: Docket Report\nCriteria: JEB\nBillable\n6 Cost: 0.60\nPages:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
